{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-134771-r4670882","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Dabeli (Potato-stuffed Buns with Chutney)","sourcePageId":134771,"sourceRevision":"4670882","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-09-18T08:28:05Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Jethwarp","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Dabeli%20(Potato-stuffed%20Buns%20with%20Chutney)&oldid=4670882","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:34.045Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Indian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using dabeli masala","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"6bd08fdf224d6245927c6aa6745d41fb53bc68b9eaf208ab2d33cc7a3738b2f3","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Servings = 2–3\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Daabeli.JPG|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Dabeli''' is an Indian dish, originally from the region Kutch in Gujarat. Dabeli is now a common street food in Mumbai. It is also called double roti or kutchi dabeli.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n===Filling===\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]] powder\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Dabeli Masala|dabeli masala]]\n* 2 medium-sized [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], boiled and mashed\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* Water\n* Green [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]] (optional), finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Peanut|peanuts]], roasted\n\n===Assembly===\n* 5–6 ladi-pav or burger buns\n* [[Cookbook:Butter|Butter]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], finely chopped\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Sev|sev]]\n* [[Cookbook:Garlic|Garlic]] [[Cookbook:Chutney|chutney]] \n* [[Cookbook:Tamarind|Tamarind]] [[Cookbook:Date|date]] chutney\n\n=== Garnish ===\n* Finely-chopped [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]]\n* 1 handful of [[Cookbook:Pomegranate|pomegranate]] seeds (optional)\n* Roasted [[Cookbook:Peanut|peanuts]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Filling ===\n# Heat oil in a pan. Add asafoetida, dabeli masala, potatoes, salt to taste, and a sprinkle of water. Mix it very well so that masala, salt and boiled potato assimilate very well.\n# Mix in the green chiles if using.\n# Remove potato mixture from the heat, and taste. If you want to make it more spicy, add some more dabeli masala, and mix again using your hands or a masher. Toss in the roasted peanuts and mix everything well.\n\n=== Assembly ===\n# [[Cookbook:Slicing|Slice]] pav/bun into halves, and toast them with a little butter on a [[Cookbook:Griddle|griddle]].\n# Apply garlic chutney to one half of the bun (inner side) and tamarind-date chutney to the other half.\n# Place a portion of the potato filling in between between the bun halves.\n\n=== Garnish ===\n# Top with chopped onion, coriander, and sev.\n#Press down the bun from both side, and garnish with pomegranate seeds, and roasted peanuts.\n#Serve immediately, while medium-hot, with a extra dip of chutney on the plate. Fried green chillies, with a sprinkle of salt can be additionally given as an add-on.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dabeli masala]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Dabeli (Potato-stuffed Buns with Chutney)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"2–3","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tablespoon oil","sourceText":"1 tablespoon oil","amountText":"1 tablespoon oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 pinch of asafoetida powder","sourceText":"1 pinch of asafoetida powder","amountText":"1 pinch of asafoetida powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 teaspoons dabeli masala","sourceText":"2 teaspoons dabeli masala","amountText":"2 teaspoons dabeli masala","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 medium-sized potatoes, boiled and mashed","sourceText":"2 medium-sized potatoes, boiled and mashed","amountText":"2 medium-sized potatoes, boiled and mashed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Water","sourceText":"Water","amountText":"Water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Green chiles (optional), finely chopped","sourceText":"Green chiles (optional), finely chopped","amountText":"Green chiles (optional), finely chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 tablespoons peanuts, roasted","sourceText":"2 tablespoons peanuts, roasted","amountText":"2 tablespoons peanuts, roasted","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"5–6 ladi-pav or burger buns","sourceText":"5–6 ladi-pav or burger buns","amountText":"5–6 ladi-pav or burger buns","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null